## 14. Conclusion

Review 2 extends the EV charging-station opportunity analysis using supervised and unsupervised machine learning. Classification Part B adds five required algorithms and compares them with the five Review 1 Part-A models. Clustering provides an unsupervised view of station groups without using the `Profit_Potential` target.

The current classification run shows Bagging with the strongest weighted F1-score among the baseline models, while Gradient Boosting provides the strongest accuracy and ROC-AUC. The clustering analysis compares K-Means and multiple Agglomerative linkage strategies using internal validation metrics and the required visualizations.
